 "lines": [
  "Your belly hair is harvesting your shirt, one fiber at a time.",
  "That lint in your belly button? Not random.",
  "A chemist in Vienna collected five hundred and three pieces of navel lint. Over three years.",
  "Mostly cotton fibers from clothes, mixed with dead skin, sweat, fat and dust.",
  "Here's the insane part. Belly hair is covered in tiny scales that act like barbed hooks.",
  "Every time you move, those scales snag fibers off your shirt.",
  "And belly hair often grows in circles around the navel, so it funnels everything into the hole.",
  "When he shaved his stomach, the lint basically stopped. Until the hair grew back.",
  "But it gets worse. That hole is the one spot almost nobody scrubs.",
  "When researchers swabbed sixty belly buttons, they found two thousand three hundred sixty eight kinds of bacteria.",
  "Around fourteen hundred might be new to science.",
  "One man carried a microbe that had only ever been found in Japan. He had never been to Japan.",
  "So you're growing a sweater and a jungle. Next time you find that fuzz, remember:",
  "Follow for a new unhinged fact every day."
 ]
